# Attribution

## This project

Unofficial, community-built Wi-Fi stack for NVIDIA Jetson Orin boards with an Intel AX210.

**This project is not published by, affiliated with, or endorsed by Intel Corporation or
NVIDIA Corporation.** For help, please use this repository's issue tracker rather than contacting
Intel, NVIDIA or the upstream projects below.

The names "Intel", "AX210", "NVIDIA", "Jetson", "Orin" and "L4T" are used solely to identify the
hardware and software this project works with.

## backport-iwlwifi

Intel's iwlwifi backport driver, GPL-2.0. Source is taken unmodified from
<https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/iwlwifi/backport-iwlwifi.git> at the commit
pinned in `versions.json`; the patches in `patches/backport-iwlwifi/` are applied at build time.
Its `COPYING` file ships in `driver-src.tar.gz` and in the built driver package.

## AX210 firmware

Copyright (c) Intel Corporation, distributed under the terms of `LICENCE.iwlwifi_firmware`.
The firmware files are taken unmodified from
<https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/firmware/linux-firmware.git> at the commit
pinned in `versions.json`, and are redistributed with that licence file.

## ell and iwd

ell and iwd are Copyright (c) Intel Corporation and contributors, mainly under LGPL-2.1+ (a
few files carry other free licences). Sources: <https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/libs/ell/ell.git>
and <https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/network/wireless/iwd.git>. The debs are built with Debian's
packaging from <https://salsa.debian.org/debian/ell.git> and
<https://salsa.debian.org/debian/iwd.git>; each deb's `debian/copyright` lists the full terms.
The matching sources are attached to every release that ships the debs.

## ell and iwd signing key

`keys/ell-iwd-signing-key.asc` is Marcel Holtmann's public key, which signs the ell and iwd
release tarballs, retrieved from kernel.org's key repository
<https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/docs/kernel/pgpkeys.git>. It is redistributed unmodified so
the signature check doesn't depend on fetching a key at build time.
